{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "d8d4f869eebc57bcf73fcab65e2bd067e18f578aab0ae6be8fbe2fe4e230a03b", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "191c72ff38ba2771b71cb9bf1211acbc5be89e96791d97f7b1db1ba0231aa599", "parent_occurrence_id": "51cf26dd5e3d1169ae07e0693a4c900fcf7777271a92717a2a7b07448ca7aba2", "source_pointer": "git:a6c62b7a220a7f8aad95266e16f9f5fe7371a486:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:0", "text": "Agent evaluations increasingly depend on context interventions---retrieval, memory graphs, and prompt contracts---yet published reports often omit null outcomes, parser failures, and negative cells."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "7b54d97bd301237be3d759c3a7019af949607ae1ac3d0b38d987fd7ac4411ab4", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "326bfe47f8f025e41fde1735971e809f18424e7715131a2b2cf3df283c291d8f", "parent_occurrence_id": "51cf26dd5e3d1169ae07e0693a4c900fcf7777271a92717a2a7b07448ca7aba2", "source_pointer": "git:a6c62b7a220a7f8aad95266e16f9f5fe7371a486:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:1", "text": "We present HydraDG, a governed experimental framework that binds substantive model invocations, tool calls, and handoffs to \\emph{Fractal Custody Objects} (FCOs) and a \\emph{Fractal Custody Graph} (FCG)."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "340870fe746d637396c8ecb935119d17baa22b94327196f282018b84b9c871b3", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "891a1aa5bb436f005b4ae31e371226334703e048461854ff5158ce5183e2fdbf", "parent_occurrence_id": "51cf26dd5e3d1169ae07e0693a4c900fcf7777271a92717a2a7b07448ca7aba2", "source_pointer": "git:a6c62b7a220a7f8aad95266e16f9f5fe7371a486:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:2", "text": "HydraDG preregisters hypotheses, freezes case manifests and scorers, records raw prompt and response hashes, and preserves terminal states including timeouts, abstentions, and malformed outputs without silent substitution."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "38260336b22929cd3e6aa7b5f260d60fdd0cc2fbc3fd2429bf4c28f7b571665c", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "ea56d3a85a66404fa05fc3379f1018d8d94ffaa818eef1f9980a23a232f7cfc0", "parent_occurrence_id": "51cf26dd5e3d1169ae07e0693a4c900fcf7777271a92717a2a7b07448ca7aba2", "source_pointer": "git:a6c62b7a220a7f8aad95266e16f9f5fe7371a486:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:3", "text": "We report two preregistered studies (EXP-008, EXP-009) comparing flat prose versus structured FCG retrieval for failure-prevention endpoints; both terminate as \\emph{underpowered} under bounded case replication, so confirmatory effect claims are not supported while negative and null evidence remains in custody."}
{"atom_type": "SENTENCE", "content_id": "5493155d2ebd8441309cae289b6961dc25f56607e972ccfbf4b375a65b4d2bdd", "hash_profile": "hydradg.longitudinal.hash_contract.v2", "occurrence_id": "d23a2baee4e5c48d30b5f25c4a4530a0e410376f2b34bf825b7e41de72b06828", "parent_occurrence_id": "51cf26dd5e3d1169ae07e0693a4c900fcf7777271a92717a2a7b07448ca7aba2", "source_pointer": "git:a6c62b7a220a7f8aad95266e16f9f5fe7371a486:paper/newinml2026_solo/final_v4/manuscript/main.tex:abstract:sent:4", "text": "We argue that custody-first evaluation infrastructure supports reproducible agent science rather than optional logging."}
